I implemented the functions in `rle.py` and `intervals.py`, and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints **ALL PASS**. The stress loop took 3.5s. I didn't change `test_impl.py`.

I ran the tests after writing the RLE functions. They got past the RLE checks and then stopped with `NotImplementedError` in `merge`, as expected. After I wrote `merge`, the whole suite passed.

- **`encode`**: groups each run of the same character and writes the character followed by its count, so `'aaabbc'` becomes `'a3b2c1'` and an empty string stays empty.
- **`decode`**: reads each non-digit character with the number after it (one or more digits) and repeats the character that many times.
- **`merge`**: sorts the intervals by start, then joins each one into the previous interval if it overlaps or just touches it, so `[1,2]` and `[2,3]` become `[1,3]`.

One limitation: `decode` can't handle text that contains digits, because the encoded output becomes ambiguous (`encode("a11")` gives `"a112"`). The docstrings don't say how to handle that and none of the tests use digits.
